    else:
        frame_streak = 1  # Content changed or expanded — reset streak!
        last_candidate = current_candidate
else:
    frame_streak = 0
    last_candidate = None

if frame_streak >= 2:
    return current_candidate  # Return the stable, byte-verified snapshot


If a node is mid-generation and appending text inside or after the frame between poll 1 and poll 2, current_candidate != last_candidate. The streak resets to 1, completely preventing early extraction!

2. Isolation to Newly Generated Assistant Messages

The _response_frame_state method already isolates new messages relative to pre-submission baseline:

Python
new_messages = messages[len(baseline):] if len(messages) > len(baseline) else []


By evaluating candidates only against new_messages, we ensure that stale frames from previous turns in the DOM tree are never evaluated.

Refined Specification Summary

Surgery #1 (Atomic Handoff): _wait_for_response returns the frozen candidate_string directly to _do_relay, bypassing _get_response DOM re-fetches.

Surgery #2 (Byte-Level Stability): The 2-poll streak requires candidate_t1 == candidate_t2 byte-for-byte on new assistant messages before declaring the frame ready.

The specification is airtight, UI-agnostic, and works identically across handshakes and relay turns.

